    "text": "this sky is guarded by the monkey and kept by mars — quick hands and a short fuse. the monkey solves the latch nobody thought was a puzzle; mars makes sure it does it now. your inner life runs fast, gets bored faster, and does its best thinking while provoking something. the room reads you as clever, which is a compliment with a lid on it. people enjoy you, quote you, and are slightly slow to trust you with anything solemn — not because you aren't deep, but because you show them the quick thing first, every time, as a reflex. a blaze-rooted moon usually has one or two people who've seen the other register, and would be startled how much those people matter to you.",
