    "text": "this sky is guarded by the horse and kept by the sun — the animal that carries kings and the light everything else is measured against. your inner life has a bearing to it. even at rest there's a carriage, a straightened spine, an instinct not to be seen flinching. the room reads you as regal, and that is a lonelier report than it sounds. people bring you their best behavior, save their mess for somebody else, and assume you're fine — because you look fine, because you have always looked fine. a throne-rooted moon has to ask to be taken care of, in plain words, and asking is the one thing the whole configuration is built to avoid.",
