    "text": "this sky is guarded by the stag and kept by the moon: the animal that carries its display on its head and sheds the whole thing every year, under the most changeable light in the sky. your inner life grows its crown, wears it, drops it, grows another. what moved you at twenty embarrasses you at thirty and you will do it again. the room reads you as warm — genuinely, immediately, correctly. what it misses is how carefully you're reading it back: you know exactly who is enjoying themselves and who is enduring the evening, and you'll adjust the room to fix it without being asked. a mane-rooted moon does emotional labor at a professional level and calls it having a good time.",
