    "text": "this sky begins a new banner: the white tiger's country ends, and your moon took root in the first station of the azure dragon, the sky of spring and beginnings. its guardian is the flood-dragon — the water-serpent that lives in the deep pool and, in the old stories, is what a dragon is before it has learned to fly. and it is jupiter-kept: the largest and most generous of the seven. so your inner life is coiled potential in deep water, and it knows it. the room reads you as impressive and unfinished — talented, obviously so, and somehow still arriving. that reading is accurate and it has an expiry date nobody will announce. a jewel-rooted moon spends its twenties being called promising and has to decide, at some point, to simply be the thing instead. the pool is not the problem. staying in it is.",
