    "text": "this sky is guarded by the leopard — the one that hunts alone and hauls what it catches up a tree to eat in peace — and it is mercury-kept. an inner life that is far more solitary than your social life suggests, and that needs its own branch to process anything on. the room reads you as everyone's friend, and that reading is not wrong so much as it is missing a whole floor. people are startled to learn how much of your life happens where they can't see it. a flock-rooted moon holds the group together and goes home alone by preference — and the ones who understand that about you without taking it personally are the ones who last.",
