    "text": "this sky's guardian is the ox, and there's a thread worth pulling here. india hung its name for this station on altair — and altair is the cowherd of the old star-story, the herdsman on one bank of the heavenly river, separated from the weaver, permitted one crossing a year. the chinese station here is named 牛, the ox, for its own stars over in capricorn; altair falls inside its stretch of sky without being one of them. two skies, one river, the same patient waiting. it is a venus-kept sky. so your inner life is patient, laboring, and organized around a distant devotion. the room reads you as unshakeable, and takes it as temperament rather than effort. what nobody sees is the waiting. a listener-rooted moon can hold a feeling in place for years without acting on it — for the right moment, the right crossing, the year the river is passable — and should be honest with themselves about which of those waits are patience and which have quietly become the point.",
