    "text": "this sky's guardian is the bat — the animal that navigates a pitch-black world by making a sound and listening to what comes back — and it is saturn-kept, slow and patient. that is a precise description of an inner life: you find out where you are by putting something out and reading the return. you learn what you think by saying it and watching the face across from you. the room reads you as easy to be around, and misses that you are constantly sounding it. a drum-rooted moon is doing more calibration per hour than almost anyone in the building, and the calibration is invisible, and the fatigue from it is real. the people worth keeping are the ones who send back a clear signal instead of an echo.",
